# Used by `docker build -f web/Dockerfile .` (BuildKit reads
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile). The context is the repo
# root, so this is an allow-list: everything is excluded, then only what the
# web image needs — the workspace manifests, packages/core and web — is let
# back in. backend/, main-web/, pdf-web/, docs/, the *-design folders, .git
# and any future app (mobile/) never reach the build.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!packages/core
!web

# ...and, inside those, nothing that is built, installed or secret.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.env*
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
web/next-env.d.ts
